        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.555,
            0.492,
            0.596
          ],
          "content": "**are (i) intersecting, then** $\\frac { a _ { 1 } } { a _ { 2 } }   \\neq   \\frac { b _ { 1 } } { b _ { 2 } }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.201,
            0.601,
            0.535,
            0.643
          ],
          "content": "**(ii) coincident, then** $\\frac{a_{1}}{a_{2}}=\\frac{b_{1}}{b_{2}}\\neq\\frac{c_{1}}{c_{2}}$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.197,
            0.645,
            0.503,
            0.688
          ],
          "content": "**(iii) parallel, then** $\\frac{a_{1}}{a_{2}}=\\frac{b_{1}}{b_{2}}\\neq\\frac{c_{1}}{c_{2}}$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.691,
            0.9,
            0.731
          ],
          "content": "**In fact, the converse is also true for any pair of lines. You can verify them by considering some more examples by yourself.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.146,
            0.734,
            0.688,
            0.754
          ],
          "content": "**Let us now consider some more examples to illustrate it.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.766,
            0.69,
            0.786
          ],
          "content": "**Example 1 : Check graphically whether the pair of equations**"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
